                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 80-year-old female admitted on 31.12.2006 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray and arterial blood gas analysis were performed, confirming exacerbation without pneumonic infiltrates. Spirometry supported the diagnosis of severe COPD. She was treated with short-acting bronchodilators via nebulisation, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement of respiratory function and symptom relief. She was discharged on 01.01.2007 in stable condition. We recommend continuation of inhaled maintenance therapy and close follow-up of pulmonary function. Please do not hesitate to contact us should any concerns arise. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
